<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Kansas, Oklahoma receive rain.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Kansas, Oklahoma receive rain.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rain fell in central and eastern Kansas and Oklahoma late Sunday and early Monday, with light showers reported in some of the dry areas of western Kansas, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>However, northwest Kansas remained dry and had 90-degree temperatures during the weekend, dealers there said.</p>
<p>Elswhere in Kansas and in central Oklahoma, dealers said 0.25 to 0.50 inch of rain fell, which was beneficial to the wheat.</p>
<p>&quot;The wheat is looking pretty good. It is all headed out,&quot; said a dealer in central Kansas. &quot;We got a lot of moisture.&quot;</p>
<p>Grain sales were slow and most basis bids were unchanged.</p>
